WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.189
Hi there!

2
00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:05.250
Who are

3
00:00:05.251 --> 00:00:08.200
you? I'm a

4
00:00:08.201 --> 00:00:11.822
polar bear. I'm a

5
00:00:11.823 --> 00:00:16.485
mammal. Where do

6
00:00:16.486 --> 00:00:19.205
you live? We live

7
00:00:19.206 --> 00:00:23.084
around the Arctic Ocean. We like

8
00:00:23.085 --> 00:00:26.888
the ice along the coast. The Arctic

9
00:00:26.889 --> 00:00:29.821
is cold! Our thick

10
00:00:29.822 --> 00:00:33.167
fur keeps us warm. Even our

11
00:00:33.168 --> 00:00:36.897
paws have fur. We also

12
00:00:36.898 --> 00:00:41.643
have a layer of fat. Can you

13
00:00:41.644 --> 00:00:44.201
swim? Polar bears

14
00:00:44.202 --> 00:00:47.796
are great swimmers! We use

15
00:00:47.797 --> 00:00:51.760
our big paws for that. We can

16
00:00:51.761 --> 00:00:56.543
swim very far. Who

17
00:00:56.544 --> 00:00:59.813
do you live with? Most

18
00:00:59.814 --> 00:01:04.136
polar bears live alone. Sometimes

19
00:01:04.137 --> 00:01:07.726
we eat together. What

20
00:01:07.727 --> 00:01:10.245
do you eat? Seals

21
00:01:10.246 --> 00:01:14.389
are our favorite food. They

22
00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:17.519
have lots of fat. We

23
00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:22.193
need fat in the cold weather.

24
00:01:22.194 --> 00:01:25.552
How do you catch seals?

25
00:01:25.553 --> 00:01:29.417
We wait next to holes in the ice.

26
00:01:29.418 --> 00:01:33.738
Seals come up for air.

27
00:01:33.739 --> 00:01:38.595
Then we attack!

28
00:01:38.596 --> 00:01:41.470
I see a hole in the ice.

29
00:01:41.471 --> 00:01:44.388
Good-bye.

30
00:01:44.389 --> 00:01:53.257
Bye, Polar Bear!

